From be7daf1a1531db3a061ed8d4453cbced0452b1b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:31:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] camera: Real photos and scene settings through
 camera-hal-bridge

On phones whose cameras come from an Android camera HAL, camera-hal-bridge
offers them as PipeWire nodes (hal_camera_<id>) whose stream carries
preview frames of 1280x720, while the sensors give up to 16 megapixels.
For these cameras the shutter asks the bridge for a real photo
(org.plinius.CameraBridge.TakePicture): the HAL shoots it through its
capture pipeline and the bridge writes the JPEG to the picture's path.
Without the bridge, or when it fails, the preview frame is stored as
before.

A scene button next to the flash button picks the HAL's scene mode (Auto,
HDR, Night, Action, Sunset, Party) and white balance, kept in the settings
and sent to the bridge with each camera picked. It shows for the bridge's
cameras only.
